                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  a \cdot (b + c)
                  \\;=\;
                  (a\cdot b) + (a\cdot c)
          %p
            and dually. Since multiplication and addition are a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decategorifications"} decategorifications
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
          %p
            More generally, one may consider arbitrary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            distributing over
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            %em not
            the same notion as limits
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutativity+of+limits+and+colimits"} commuting
            with colimits, although in some cases they are related (see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permuting+limits+and+colimits"} permuting limits and colimits
            for more).
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %h3#explicitly_using_limits_and_colimits Explicitly using limits and colimits
          %p
            Given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+categories"} small categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi I
                  %mo ×
                  %mi K
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  D \,\colon\, I \times K \longrightarrow C
          %p
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            that admits all necessary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            we have a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi colim
                    %mi K
                  %msub
                    %mi lim
                    %mi I
                  %mi D
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi lim
                    %mi I
                  %msub
                    %mi colim
                    %mi K
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f
                  \\,\colon\,
                  colim_K lim_I D
                  \\longrightarrow
                  lim_I colim_K D
          %p
            induced using the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi colim
                    %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} colim_K
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi lim
                    %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} lim_I
            by the family of composites
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi lim
                    %mi I
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi colim
                    %mi K
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  lim_I D(-,k)
                  \\longrightarrow
                  D(i,k)
                  \\longrightarrow
                  colim_K D(i,-)
          %p
            of the limit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i\in I
            and the colimit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coprojection"} injection
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k\in K
          %p
            Recall that
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            are said to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutativity+of+limits+and+colimits"} commute
            with
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            if and only if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
          %p
            Now we note that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            factors as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi colim
                    %mi K
                  %msub
                    %mi lim
                    %mi I
                  %mi D
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi g
                  %msub
                    %mi colim
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi K
                        %mi I
                  %msub
                    %mi lim
                    %mi I
                  %mi D
                  %mo ′
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi h
                  %msub
                    %mi lim
                    %mi I
                  %msub
                    %mi colim
                    %mi K
                  %mi D
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} colim_K lim_I D \xrightarrow{g} colim_{K^I} lim_I D' \xrightarrow{h} lim_I colim_K D.
          %p
            Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi K
                    %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^I
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi I
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi K
                    %mi I
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D'\colon I\times K^I\to C
            is obtained from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/precomposition"} precomposition
            with the functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ev
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi I
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi K
                    %mi I
                  %mo →
                  %mi I
                  %mo ×
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\pi_1,ev) : I\times K^I \to I\times K
            that sends a pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i,s)
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i,s(i))
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            is induced by the diagonal functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi K
                    %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K\to K^I
            sending each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            to the corresponding
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+functor"} constant functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
            is defined by the universal properties of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi colim
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi K
                        %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} colim_{K^I}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi lim
                    %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} lim_I
            from the family of composites
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi lim
                    %mi I
                  %mi D
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi colim
                    %mi K
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} lim_I D'(-,s) \to D'(i,s) = D(i,s(i)) \to colim_K D(i,-)
          %p
            of the limit projection for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i\in I
            and the colimit injection for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c(i)\in K
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              \-limits distribute over
              = succeed "-colimits" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
            is an isomorphism for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
          %p
            More generally, we can allow
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            to vary with
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi I
                    %mo →
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K\colon I\to Cat
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi K
                    %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^I
            we use the limit category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi lim
                      %mi I
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} lim_I K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            is defined on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+colimit"}> lax colimit
            )
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi I
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int^I K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+functor"} constant functor
          %p
          #DistributivityOfProductsOverSums.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              In the simple example
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo +
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \times (B + C) \cong (A \times B) + (A \times C)
              alluded to in the introduction,
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                  is a two-element
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+category"} discrete category
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(0)
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+category"} terminal category
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(1)
                  is again a two-element discrete category.
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi I
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int^I K
              is a three-element discrete category, and the diagram
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi I
                    %mi K
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \colon \int^I K \to \mathcal{C}
              picks the objects
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒦
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{K}
            is a class of small categories rather than a single one, we say that
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              \-limits distribute over
              = succeed "-colimits" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒦
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{K}
            in a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            if the corresponding map is an isomorphism for any
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi I
                  %mo →
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \,\colon\, I\to Cat
            taking values in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒦
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{K}
            = succeed "For" do
              %br/
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒦
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{K}
            is the class of all
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+categories"} discrete categories
            = succeed "-limits" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
          %p
            If instead
            = succeed "-limits" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            = succeed "-colimits" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒦
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K\in \mathcal{K}
            = succeed "-limits" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            = succeed "-limits.\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
          .standout
            %p The author of the previous paragraph doesn’t know whether distributivity over uniform colimits is actually any weaker, but if it is, then the non-uniform version seems more correct.
          %h3#for_kan_extensions For Kan extensions
          %p
            Yet more generally, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mo :
                  %mi I
                  %mo →
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u : I\to J
            be any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+fibration"} Grothendieck fibration
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                  %mo :
                  %mi K
                  %mo →
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v : K\to I
            a Grothendieck opfibration. Since fibrations are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponentiable+functors"} exponentiable functors
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributivity+pullback"} distributivity pullback
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi p
                        %mtd
                          %mi K
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi v
                        %mtd
                          %mi I
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo
                            %mi q
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi u
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi r
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \array{ X &amp; \xrightarrow{p} &amp; K &amp; \xrightarrow{v} &amp; I \\ ^q\downarrow &amp;&amp;&amp;&amp; \downarrow^u \\ Y &amp;&amp; \xrightarrow{r} &amp;&amp; J }
          %p
            Thus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product"} dependent product
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mi I
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_I K
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi J
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mi I
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = I\times_J \Pi_I K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:X\to K
            is “evaluation”. Now in any sufficiently complete category, there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beck-Chevalley"} Beck-Chevalley
            isomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mo *
                  %mo ∘
                  %msub
                    %mi Ran
                    %mi u
                  %mo ≅
                  %msub
                    %mi Ran
                    %mi q
                  %mo ∘
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mo *
                  %mo ∘
                  %msup
                    %mi v
                    %mo *
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r^* \circ Ran_u \cong Ran_q \circ p^* \circ v^*.
          %p
            This is because any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            of a fibration is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+square"} exact square
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mate"} mate
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Lan
                    %mi r
                  %mo ∘
                  %msub
                    %mi Ran
                    %mi q
                  %mo ∘
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Ran
                    %mi u
                  %mo ∘
                  %msub
                    %mi Lan
                    %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Lan_r \circ Ran_q \circ p^* \to Ran_u \circ Lan_v
          %p
            and we say that
            %strong
              right Kan extensions along
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
              distribute over left Kan extensions along
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
            if this mate is an isomorphism.
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J=1
            then this reduces to the above non-uniform notion, where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo →
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K\to I
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
            of a functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo →
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I\to Cat
            = succeed "-diagrams" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
            distribute over left Kan extensions along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
            if and only if the above non-uniform distributivity condition holds for the fibers of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
            over each object of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
          %p
            The formulation in terms of Kan extensions generalizes naturally to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivators"} derivators
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internalized
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+categories"} internal categories
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations"} fibrations
            in any
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+category"} locally cartesian closed category
          %h3#for_sound_doctrines For sound doctrines
          %p
            (See Section 6 in
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "#ABLR"} ABLR
          %p
            Given a
            = succeed "\u00A0" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sound+doctrine"} sound doctrine
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            of limits, we have the associated notions of
            = succeed "-limits," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            = succeed "-filtered" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            = succeed "-filtered" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo −
                  %mi Ind
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D-Ind(C)
            of a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            together with the associated colimit functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi colim
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi D
                    %mo −
                    %mi Ind
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} colim\colon D-Ind(C)\to C
          %p
            We say that some class of limits
            %em
              distributes over
              = succeed "-filtered" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            if the functor colim preserves these limits.
          %p
            See Appendix A in
            %a{:href => "#AR"} AR
            for a comparison of this definition to the above explicit definition in the special case of distributivity of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimits"} filtered colimits
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+limits"} small limits
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+finitely+presentable+categories"} locally finitely presentable categories
            and distributivity of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sifted+colimits"} sifted colimits
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+limits"} small limits
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/varieties+of+algebras"} varieties of algebras
          %h2#relation_to_commutativity_of_limits_and_colimits Relation to commutativity of limits and colimits
          %p
            Observe that distributivity is asymmetric with respect to limits and colimits, whereas
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutativity+of+limits+and+colimits"} commutativity of limits and colimits
            is a symmetric notion. In some cases, however, distributivity and commutativity are equivalent. This happens exactly when the above functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            is an isomorphism, which is to say that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal"} diagonal
            map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi K
                    %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K\to K^I
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/final+functor"} final functor
          %p Thus, for instance, finite limits distribute over (uniform) filtered colimits if and only if finite limits commute with filtered colimits. The same is true for finite products and sifted colimits.
          %h2#distributivity_of_1limits_over_1colimits Distributivity of (∞,1)-limits over (∞,1)-colimits
          %p
            The condition that small
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limits"} (∞,1)-limits
            distribute over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-filtered+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimits"} (∞,1)-filtered (∞,1)-colimits
            precisely characterizes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+assembled+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} compactly assembled (∞,1)-categories
            among all
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} presentable (∞,1)-categories
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#finite_products Finite products
          %p
            The distributivity of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+products"} finite products
            over arbitrary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
            is the most classical version. See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributivity+for+monoidal+structures"} distributivity for monoidal structures
            for various generalizations.
          %p
            More generally, finite products distribute over arbitrary colimits in any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          %h3#filtered_colimits Filtered colimits
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            is the doctrine of finite limits, then
            = succeed "-filtered" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            = succeed "-filtered" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ind
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ind(C)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ind-objects"} Ind-objects
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            According to Definition 5.11 in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#ALR"} ALR
            %em precontinuous
            if it admits small limits and filtered colimits, and the functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi colim
                  %mo :
                  %mi Ind
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} colim: Ind(C)\to C
            is continuous.
          %p
            According to Theorem 2.1 in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#ARVloc"} ARVloc
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimits"} filtered colimits
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimits"} filtered colimits
            commute with finite
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
            distribute over
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimits"} filtered colimits
          %p
            In particular, any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+finitely+presentable+category"} locally finitely presentable category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+algebraic+theory"} essentially algebraic theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#ALR"} ALR
          %p
            In fact, as shown in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#ALR"} ALR
            %span.newWikiWord
              equational hull
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/equational+hull"} ?
            of the bicategory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+finitely+presentable+categories"} locally finitely presentable categories
            and continuous functors that preserve filtered colimits.
          %h3#sifted_colimits Sifted colimits
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            is the doctrine of finite products, then
            = succeed "-filtered" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sifted+colimits"} sifted colimits
            and the
            = succeed "-filtered" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sind-object"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sind
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sind(C)
            %span.newWikiWord
              nonabelian derived category
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/nonabelian+derived+category"} ?
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            According to Definition 4.5 in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#ALRalg"} ALRalg
            %em algebraically exact
            if it admits small limits and sifted colimits, and the functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi colim
                  %mo :
                  %mi Sind
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} colim: Sind(C)\to C
            is continuous. In particular (Example 5.3 in
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#ALRalg"} ALRalg
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variety+of+algebras"} variety of algebras
            is an algebraically exact category. In particular, this includes
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          %p
            In fact, as shown in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#ALRalg"} ALRalg
            %span.newWikiWord
              equational hull
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/equational+hull"} ?
            of the bicategory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/varieties+of+algebras"} varieties of algebras
            and continuous functors that preserve sifted colimits.
          %h3#indexed_products_and_coproducts Indexed products and coproducts
          %p
            When the definition for Kan extensions is internalized to internal categories and fibrations, and then specialized to the case of discrete categories, the notion of distributivity of dependent products over dependent sums encoded by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributivity+pullback"} distributivity pullback
            becomes the statement that in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain+fibration"} codomain fibration
            %span.newWikiWord
              indexed products
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/indexed+products"} ?
            distribute over
            %span.newWikiWord
              indexed coproducts
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/indexed+coproducts"} ?
            in this sense.
          %h3#PullbackStableColimits Pullback-stable colimits
          %p
